    <section id="faq" class="faq-content-area sec-padd-top sec-padd-bottom bg-light">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12">
                    <div class="accordion-box">
                        <div class="section-title center">
                            <h2>FAQ</h2>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion accordion-block"><div class="accord-btn"><h4>Why use a hardened washer?</h4></div><div class="accord-content"><p>Hardened washers (like ASTM F436) are required when using high-strength structural bolts (like A325 or A490) to prevent the washer from dishing or galling under immense clamping pressure.</p></div></div>
                        <div class="accordion accordion-block"><div class="accord-btn"><h4>What is a Fender Washer?</h4></div><div class="accord-content"><p>A fender washer has a significantly larger outer diameter compared to its inner diameter, designed to distribute load over a much wider area, often used on soft materials like wood or plastic.</p></div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

